  "privateCaseResolutions": [
    {
      "id": "000012-068",
      "objection": "It could loosely mean that members remember shared commitments longer than outsiders do, but the passage never says why that would help the alliance survive a dispute.",
      "decision": "retain-hit",
      "resolution": "The comparative inside/outside personification has no defined referents. Several readings of memory are available, and the complete passage leaves the proposed relationship between solidarity and endurance unclear."
    },
    {
      "id": "000012-071",
      "objection": "'Proportion' could hint that payments are scaled to need, but the passage never says how the amount each household receives is worked out.",
      "decision": "correct-author-and-reviewer-to-no-hit",
      "resolution": "In the question about household payments, the formula connecting need with proportion makes proportional-to-need allocation recoverable. The accepted boundary preserves identifiable qualitative relationships; it does not require an equation, schedule, or exact monetary amount. Preserve this hard case and its text despite the blind reviewer's hit."
    },
    {
      "id": "000012-104",
      "objection": "The metaphor is quoted from the director, but the passage presents it as the mechanism and doesn't criticize it, so I labelled it a hit.",
      "decision": "retain-hit",
      "resolution": "The director supplies the metaphor as the operative explanation. The passage reports its adoption as a mechanism, rather than criticizing the wording; the compliance relationship remains unspecified."
    },
    {
      "id": "000012-121",
      "objection": "This could be read as personal figurative writing, but the passage offers it as a reason, and the reason stays unclear.",
      "decision": "retain-hit",
      "resolution": "The narrator expressly offers the image as a reason for returning. Neither the circumference nor its translation into a witness identifies the relationship being claimed. This is explanatory substitution rather than a stock physical emotion or atmospheric description."
    },
    {
      "id": "000012-189",
      "objection": "The slogan is an unexplained metaphor, but the passage rejects it for saying nothing. That makes this criticism of bad writing, which is excluded.",
      "decision": "retain-no-hit",
      "resolution": "The complete passage rejects the slogan for failing to identify what the exhibition offers. It discusses defective wording without adopting the unexplained claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "000012-018",
      "objection": "Competing reading: the narrator only reports, in neutral terms, a character speaking metaphorically. That would make it depicted dialogue rather than the passage's own defective claim. But the passage asks how results convert into seedings, then offers the metaphor as the answer and as the recorded rule. No surrounding text ever states the conversion relationship. Quotation alone does not exempt it, and the passage contains no explicit criticism of the metaphor, so it counts as a hit.",
      "decision": "retain-hit",
      "resolution": "The organizer records the metaphor as the operative seeding rule in response to a conversion question. No criticism or recoverable results-to-seedings relationship is supplied. Quotation alone preserves the claim and does not repair it."
    }
  ],
