        "id": "000012-169",
        "decision": "retain-corrected-no-hit",
        "resolution": "The fresh reviewer expressly recovers the relationship that member votes set limits on expert advice, then requires a dispute-settlement procedure. The accepted definition requires an identifiable relationship, which the river/shore mapping supplies. Preserve the original text with a no-hit label.",
        "objection": "One could read the river and shore image as 'members' votes set the limits on expert advice'. But it never says who decides what or how a disagreement is settled. The fees and meeting venue don't fill that gap."
      },
      {
        "id": "000012-071",
        "decision": "retain-original-hard-no-hit",
        "resolution": "The amount question makes need and proportion a recoverable payment relationship. No second allocation basis is stated. Requiring weights, an equation, or exact amounts adds a procedural-completeness requirement outside this check. Preserve the original no-hit and text.",
        "objection": "One could read this as 'the formula blends need-based and proportional allocation'. But it never says how much each household gets, how the two are weighted, or what 'pays attention to the answer' does."
      }
    ],
